1
00:00:00,478 --> 00:00:03,652
Reach your hands out,

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:06,913
cut through the wind,

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,130
and forge ahead, drawing your own map as you go!

4
00:00:16,435 --> 00:00:19,565
We can't even tell left from right

5
00:00:19,608 --> 00:00:22,782
in this tempest-tossed era

6
00:00:22,869 --> 00:00:26,043
Even the values we've honed

7
00:00:26,043 --> 00:00:29,390
seem ready to crumble

8
00:00:29,391 --> 00:00:32,652
Is the compass leading us true,

9
00:00:32,696 --> 00:00:35,869
or is it leading us astray?

10
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:39,217
Nobody knows for sure!

11
00:00:39,217 --> 00:00:45,652
Just breathe deep, close your eyes

12
00:00:45,739 --> 00:00:52,696
and you'll find your soul guiding the way!

13
00:00:52,739 --> 00:00:55,913
Reach your hands out,

14
00:00:55,913 --> 00:00:59,174
cut through the wind,

15
00:00:59,174 --> 00:01:04,043
and kick away the darkness!

16
00:01:05,086 --> 00:01:08,129
I'm doing this for myself,

17
00:01:08,130 --> 00:01:12,260
and you're doing this for yourself too, right?

18
00:01:12,347 --> 00:01:17,347
Forge ahead, painting the world in your own colors!

19
00:01:25,565 --> 00:01:27,999
I'm gonna roast ya!

20
00:01:29,347 --> 00:01:31,217
Til you're well-done!

21
00:01:32,957 --> 00:01:35,348
Gonna mince ya!

22
00:01:52,086 --> 00:01:54,738
Please take me straight to the castle!

23
00:01:54,739 --> 00:01:59,304
What's the matter, Izo,
making me carry an injured man?

24
00:02:00,347 --> 00:02:01,260
Sorry.

25
00:02:02,043 --> 00:02:03,260
But that earlier news...

26
00:02:03,869 --> 00:02:08,173
...about a giant specter appearing
on the second floor caused me some alarm.

27
00:02:08,565 --> 00:02:10,608
Yeah, where'd it even come from?

28
00:02:11,957 --> 00:02:13,696
I heard the castle is ablaze.

29
00:02:17,478 --> 00:02:19,174
Don't let up then, yeah?

30
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:21,000
Aye!

31
00:02:30,521 --> 00:02:33,173
Get moving!
The monster's coming!

32
00:02:33,174 --> 00:02:35,652
Those damn samurai
are blocking the exit!

33
00:02:36,217 --> 00:02:38,652
Cannon... Bring a cannon!

34
00:02:38,739 --> 00:02:42,869
The castle's a living hell!
Secure an exit!

35
00:02:42,869 --> 00:02:44,999
Stupid samurai...
kick their asses!

36
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,478
Get outta here, or we're all toast!

37
00:02:54,391 --> 00:02:58,087
It's a great deal for ya,
Young Master Yamato!

38
00:02:58,696 --> 00:03:01,261
Just hear me oooout!

39
00:03:04,869 --> 00:03:07,999
Apoo, at it again!

40
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,174
And now you're thinking you're going to
gain favor with Yamato, are you?!

41
00:03:11,217 --> 00:03:13,260
I'm talkin' to you,
Young Master!

42
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,564
Stop, Apoo!

43
00:03:14,608 --> 00:03:17,912
I told you, I am occupied!
Do not follow me!

44
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,130
Fuga!

45
00:03:24,217 --> 00:03:26,913
It has been a while...
But I am pressed for time!

46
00:03:29,086 --> 00:03:32,173
Now is not the time
for frolicking around...

47
00:03:32,217 --> 00:03:35,043
Castle Second Floor to all floors:

48
00:03:36,913 --> 00:03:40,304
The giant flaming specter
is headed underground!

49
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,652
Hm? A cushion?

50
00:03:48,652 --> 00:03:50,652
No, this is...

51
00:03:51,043 --> 00:03:52,738
...a head of hair.

52
00:03:52,739 --> 00:03:53,609
Whose, though?!

53
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:57,086
Here they come!

54
00:03:57,086 --> 00:03:58,043
Indeed.

55
00:03:59,696 --> 00:04:00,565
You cannot run!

56
00:04:03,696 --> 00:04:04,826
Fight it is, then!

57
00:04:09,478 --> 00:04:10,130
Eh?

58
00:04:16,521 --> 00:04:18,956
What... is that?!

59
00:04:18,957 --> 00:04:20,739
A ball of flame?

60
00:04:20,739 --> 00:04:21,869
A nuisance...

61
00:04:32,217 --> 00:04:33,434
What's that?!

62
00:04:33,435 --> 00:04:35,826
So huuuuge!

63
00:04:36,739 --> 00:04:39,609
The flame specter's intentions
remain unknown!

64
00:04:42,478 --> 00:04:45,304
Fuga, run! It comes!

65
00:04:46,217 --> 00:04:50,174
The flame specter is descending!

66
00:04:51,913 --> 00:04:53,260
I repeat:

67
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:55,782
It is descending!

68
00:05:24,739 --> 00:05:26,130
Is that what happens...

69
00:05:26,913 --> 00:05:29,478
...when he pulls on his crest?!

70
00:05:30,435 --> 00:05:32,130
What the hell is he up to?

71
00:05:33,174 --> 00:05:35,217
Imperial Deep Pride...

72
00:05:35,739 --> 00:05:36,435
...Stake!

73
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:45,564
Is it unblockable?!
It's basically a damn laser!

74
00:05:48,391 --> 00:05:51,391
In ancient times,
this is how the pteranodon...

75
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,174
...hunted its prey!

76
00:06:00,130 --> 00:06:03,087
Dammit, didn't know that!

77
00:06:16,391 --> 00:06:20,304
I've gotta land a hit on him somehow,
or all I'm gonna do is tire myself out!

78
00:06:21,043 --> 00:06:24,869
Don't tell me that flame on his back
also comes with being a pteranodon!

79
00:06:27,043 --> 00:06:30,174
It doesn't!

80
00:06:33,086 --> 00:06:35,999
Who does he think he is,
talking to me from up there!

81
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,174
First things first:
knock him out of the sky!

82
00:06:56,435 --> 00:06:57,956
Three-Sword Style:

83
00:06:57,957 --> 00:07:01,217
Kalasutra:
Grand Dragon Twister!

84
00:07:17,957 --> 00:07:21,391
What the hell is up with this guy's
weird-ass toughness?!

85
00:07:21,957 --> 00:07:26,130
Guess dragons and dinos both
soak up damage like nobody's business, huh?

86
00:07:26,521 --> 00:07:28,130
That's right.

87
00:07:28,130 --> 00:07:32,260
But in my case, it goes even beyond that.
You could say I'm a little unique.

88
00:07:35,391 --> 00:07:37,826
I'll give you the
sword fight you want!

89
00:07:37,826 --> 00:07:39,695
I like swords, too.

90
00:07:50,696 --> 00:07:53,217
I've slashed him
more than a few times.

91
00:07:53,217 --> 00:07:54,478
Ultra...

92
00:07:56,739 --> 00:07:58,174
Tiger Hunt!

93
00:08:00,304 --> 00:08:02,738
But he ain't bleeding.

94
00:08:02,739 --> 00:08:04,087
He can flap his wings.

95
00:08:05,826 --> 00:08:09,173
They're not just for show,
but I can't be sure he can fly with them.

96
00:08:13,043 --> 00:08:16,129
The flame on his back
is still burning...

97
00:08:16,652 --> 00:08:20,217
Thought that was part of
his Devil Fruit power, but guess not.

98
00:08:20,739 --> 00:08:23,956
Maybe he's got Fishman
or Giant's blood in him?

99
00:08:24,608 --> 00:08:28,217
Guess it's some race
I've never heard of...

100
00:08:28,217 --> 00:08:32,565
You're searching for answers...
Your eyes betray your confusion!

101
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,565
If this keeps up...

102
00:08:44,347 --> 00:08:46,608
...and I can't figure out what he is...

103
00:08:47,521 --> 00:08:48,782
I don't think...

104
00:08:50,130 --> 00:08:51,217
...can...

105
00:08:55,739 --> 00:08:58,000
...beat him.

106
00:09:15,565 --> 00:09:17,260
What's that sound?

107
00:09:20,739 --> 00:09:24,609
A shamisen? Ain't no way...

108
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,130
The hell is happening?!

109
00:09:48,174 --> 00:09:50,000
Enma's...!

110
00:09:56,435 --> 00:09:57,913
What is this?

111
00:10:01,174 --> 00:10:03,304
The sound of a shamisen?

112
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,087
Impossible...

113
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,391
In the midst of battle?
What trickery is this?!

114
00:10:10,869 --> 00:10:12,695
Is it coming from
the room next door?

115
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:16,260
I-Is it the enemy?

116
00:10:19,608 --> 00:10:21,608
Who is it?

117
00:10:21,608 --> 00:10:25,521
No one could possibly
be holding a feast right now...

118
00:10:26,521 --> 00:10:29,521
It's so bright...
I can't see...

119
00:10:41,521 --> 00:10:43,782
Ko... Komu...

120
00:10:44,696 --> 00:10:48,652
Komurasaki!

121
00:10:51,478 --> 00:10:53,348
Is this the afterlife?

122
00:10:54,130 --> 00:10:56,043
Or is this a dream?

123
00:10:58,086 --> 00:11:03,043
Since that day, not a night has passed
that I don't dream about you.

124
00:11:03,782 --> 00:11:06,999
How could I possibly forget you!

125
00:11:07,521 --> 00:11:09,260
I cannot forget you, either...

126
00:11:09,652 --> 00:11:10,565
...milord.

127
00:11:15,217 --> 00:11:19,304
Tam, and always shall be,
by your side.

128
00:11:22,565 --> 00:11:26,260
If this is a dream,
I don't want to wake up!

129
00:11:50,739 --> 00:11:52,826
What is that?!
It passes through the walls!

130
00:12:05,913 --> 00:12:10,304
To the abyss...

131
00:12:14,086 --> 00:12:15,912
Shoot, shoot!

132
00:12:19,869 --> 00:12:23,304
I repeat, Castle Second Floor
to all floors:

133
00:12:23,304 --> 00:12:27,912
The flame specter continues
its descent underground!

134
00:12:31,086 --> 00:12:31,999
"Descent"?!

135
00:12:33,217 --> 00:12:34,826
That mustn't happen!

136
00:12:34,826 --> 00:12:38,173
If it keeps descending,
it will reach the armory!

137
00:12:40,608 --> 00:12:43,217
Should that come to pass,

138
00:12:43,217 --> 00:12:46,043
it will ignite
the massive pile of gunpowder!

139
00:12:49,260 --> 00:12:50,695
I must hurry!

140
00:12:50,696 --> 00:12:51,435
Fuga!

141
00:12:51,869 --> 00:12:53,956
I want you to help me
with something!

142
00:12:55,217 --> 00:12:57,260
This way!
Come with me!

143
00:12:58,260 --> 00:12:59,217
Whoa!

144
00:13:00,130 --> 00:13:05,130
What I would give for a moment's respite
upon this wonderful, soft bed,

145
00:13:06,478 --> 00:13:08,782
but we ought to be off.

146
00:13:13,043 --> 00:13:15,738
The CPo agents are
just beyond the flames!

147
00:13:15,739 --> 00:13:18,913
And they'll be after us before we know it!
Let's not tarry, then!

148
00:13:47,608 --> 00:13:48,521
Nico Robin...

149
00:13:49,826 --> 00:13:51,782
You cannot run from us...!

150
00:14:00,043 --> 00:14:03,695
Smile! I'm taking
a commemorative photo for you!

151
00:14:03,696 --> 00:14:07,304
"Pets of the Celestial Dragons
at Kaido's Castle!"

152
00:14:07,826 --> 00:14:11,391
This's a scoop!

153
00:14:14,957 --> 00:14:19,087
Maybe I'll sell this story to Morgans,
from the World Economic Journal!

154
00:14:22,391 --> 00:14:24,260
I can see the headlines now:

155
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:27,999
"The Government, After Losing
Their Broker Doflamingo,

156
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,652
Finally..."

157
00:14:48,521 --> 00:14:49,825
Hey! Apoo?!

158
00:14:53,826 --> 00:14:55,521
X. Drake...

159
00:14:56,086 --> 00:14:59,303
Do you think we don't know
who you really are?

160
00:14:59,739 --> 00:15:02,217
Go ahead, try coming up
with a cover story!

161
00:15:07,521 --> 00:15:09,304
Inconveniences...

162
00:15:15,347 --> 00:15:16,390
...must be erased.

163
00:15:18,957 --> 00:15:20,783
Boom!

164
00:15:28,217 --> 00:15:29,739
Dammit!

165
00:15:29,739 --> 00:15:34,130
That hurt, you stupid ass
Government assassins!

166
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:39,521
Oh, you're alive.

167
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:40,825
Shaddap!

168
00:15:40,826 --> 00:15:43,347
What, ya think I wouldn't
use Armament Haki, dumbass?!

169
00:15:43,696 --> 00:15:46,217
I'll make them pay for that!

170
00:15:48,565 --> 00:15:51,434
And you're Navy, aren't ya?!

171
00:15:52,130 --> 00:15:53,391
Mouth shut.

172
00:15:53,478 --> 00:15:55,739
Are we doing this or not?

173
00:15:55,739 --> 00:15:58,391
Well, they started it!

174
00:15:58,739 --> 00:16:00,347
No, you did.

175
00:16:00,347 --> 00:16:03,912
We're absolutely doing this!

176
00:16:33,347 --> 00:16:34,956
Why's it suddenly...?!

177
00:16:36,304 --> 00:16:38,390
Enma!

178
00:16:38,739 --> 00:16:44,652
Who said you could
unleash yourself without my permission?!

179
00:16:49,130 --> 00:16:50,260
What's wrong?

180
00:16:52,521 --> 00:16:53,869
Having a falling out?

181
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:09,260
Nuh?!

182
00:17:29,521 --> 00:17:31,260
What're you trying now?!

183
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,782
I'll give you a chance.

184
00:17:35,913 --> 00:17:37,783
Do what you want.

185
00:17:40,217 --> 00:17:41,652
Don't you look down on me!

186
00:17:52,086 --> 00:17:52,999
Direct hit!

187
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,174
Huh?!

188
00:18:05,957 --> 00:18:09,609
That was the Pirate Hunter
you had on the Snail, wasn't it?!

189
00:18:10,521 --> 00:18:13,043
Ain't no way
he's winnin' against King!

190
00:18:20,086 --> 00:18:21,086
Close call...

191
00:18:22,913 --> 00:18:25,261
If my Color of Arms was any slower,
I would've been toast...

192
00:18:38,652 --> 00:18:43,174
From the size of that blast,
it was almost like he was trying to kill both of us!

193
00:18:43,782 --> 00:18:46,130
How in the hell
is he still alive?!

194
00:18:46,782 --> 00:18:50,565
That was a straight-up suicide attack!

195
00:18:53,435 --> 00:18:57,608
He's one of the last remaining Lunarians,
a survivor of a race thought to be wiped out!

196
00:18:57,608 --> 00:19:02,217
A race of monsters,
able to survive in any environment!

197
00:19:02,217 --> 00:19:07,347
Long ago, folks called 'em "gods"!

198
00:19:07,782 --> 00:19:10,565
How'd they end up wiped out?

199
00:19:10,565 --> 00:19:12,825
Huh?! That's something...

200
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:17,086
...you oughta look up
in a history book!

201
00:19:29,521 --> 00:19:31,608
One-Sword Style, Draw:

202
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,435
Death...

203
00:19:39,478 --> 00:19:41,391
...Lion Song!

204
00:20:13,043 --> 00:20:15,347
Not even a damn scratch?!

205
00:20:16,869 --> 00:20:19,826
That attack was way stronger
than the others!

206
00:20:27,130 --> 00:20:28,130
A shamisen?

207
00:20:36,260 --> 00:20:37,912
Whoa, wait, Enma!

208
00:20:38,608 --> 00:20:41,521
Imperial Deep Pride Stake!

209
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,522
Not now, Enma!

210
00:21:05,608 --> 00:21:09,738
First time I've seen a swordsman
held back by his own sword!

211
00:21:14,826 --> 00:21:16,739
Kitetsu III!

212
00:21:27,086 --> 00:21:28,434
A cursed sword, huh?!

213
00:21:28,435 --> 00:21:30,782
YYou idiot,
it ain't for sale!

214
00:21:30,782 --> 00:21:35,478
If you die using it,
it'd be like I done the deed myself!

215
00:21:35,478 --> 00:21:37,130
How 'bout this, then?

216
00:21:52,608 --> 00:21:54,217
I'm taking it.

217
00:21:58,304 --> 00:22:01,260
My, how Kitetsu's countenance
has changed!

218
00:22:02,174 --> 00:22:05,434
It would seem it has finally found
the hands of a worthy owner!

219
00:22:06,435 --> 00:22:10,782
The Kitetsu III you wield
is of my design.

220
00:22:10,782 --> 00:22:12,521
That true?!

221
00:22:16,913 --> 00:22:18,826
You going to die,
just to save your sword?

222
00:22:44,913 --> 00:22:45,609
Hot!

223
00:22:51,957 --> 00:22:55,087
Oh, good. It didn't fall off.

224
00:22:56,869 --> 00:22:58,912
Wado Ichimonji...

225
00:23:03,478 --> 00:23:07,000
Sensei!
Let me have her sword!

226
00:23:07,782 --> 00:23:09,347
Aye, very well.

227
00:23:13,435 --> 00:23:17,000
I'm gonna get stronger,
for both of us!

228
00:23:17,565 --> 00:23:20,825
I'm gonna get so strong,
the heavens'll know my name!

229
00:23:20,826 --> 00:23:24,391
I'm gonna be
the world's strongest swordsman!

230
00:23:24,391 --> 00:23:25,608
Boy!

231
00:23:25,608 --> 00:23:28,130
Enma, the blade Hiyori-sama
bestowed upon you...

232
00:23:28,130 --> 00:23:31,087
Does it perhaps feel
strangely familiar in your grasp?

233
00:23:31,957 --> 00:23:34,652
It works much like
any cursed blade.

234
00:23:34,652 --> 00:23:37,696
The weak cannot handle them.

235
00:23:37,696 --> 00:23:42,565
But the most important reason
it has molded itself to your hand, by twist of fate,

236
00:23:42,565 --> 00:23:48,086
is that Wado Ichimonji and Enma
were forged by the same person!

237
00:23:48,086 --> 00:23:51,825
The artisan,
Shimotsuki Kozaburo!

238
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:05,087
It all happened so fast,
I never really stopped to think about it...

239
00:24:08,826 --> 00:24:12,260
But how'd a sword from Wano...

240
00:24:12,260 --> 00:24:14,825
...end up in the backwaters
of the East Blue?

241
00:24:51,869 --> 00:24:54,173
Completed your three-sword set?

242
00:24:54,696 --> 00:24:57,174
Imperial Slings and Arrows!

243
00:25:00,739 --> 00:25:02,087
Enma!

244
00:25:27,347 --> 00:25:28,782
Enma...

245
00:25:29,478 --> 00:25:32,869
A sword from the Land of Wano...

246
00:25:35,782 --> 00:25:38,869
A sword from Wano!

247
00:25:41,521 --> 00:25:42,956
Zorojuro.

248
00:25:43,957 --> 00:25:45,565
The word "Sunacchi"...

249
00:25:46,478 --> 00:25:49,217
I was warned to never say it.

250
00:25:49,217 --> 00:25:53,391
learned it from an old man in my village
a long time ago.

251
00:25:53,826 --> 00:25:56,130
Never said it, either.

252
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:58,739
What?!

253
00:26:00,913 --> 00:26:02,565
An old man in the village?!

254
00:26:13,391 --> 00:26:16,782
That old man
who was always on the sea coast...

255
00:26:18,391 --> 00:26:20,043
For the longest time,

256
00:26:21,304 --> 00:26:22,782
I didn't know his name.

257
00:26:36,478 --> 00:26:38,391
Not there!

258
00:26:38,391 --> 00:26:39,695
Go, go!

259
00:26:39,696 --> 00:26:41,826
That's the spirit, Zoro!

260
00:27:08,869 --> 00:27:10,391
Sunacchi!

261
00:27:10,739 --> 00:27:13,956
'Tis a word for good luck,
raises the spirit!

262
00:27:14,478 --> 00:27:18,043
Huh...
I dun need it.

263
00:27:18,043 --> 00:27:20,216
Funny word.

264
00:27:20,217 --> 00:27:21,695
Anyway, old man,

265
00:27:21,696 --> 00:27:24,304
you were a Samurai, weren'tcha?

266
00:27:25,217 --> 00:27:27,304
Everyone at the dojo said so.

267
00:27:27,826 --> 00:27:28,999
Best they hold their tongues!

268
00:27:29,435 --> 00:27:32,521
Lest the Navy be upon us.

269
00:27:34,391 --> 00:27:37,086
The Navy?! Why?!

270
00:27:37,086 --> 00:27:38,521
I will not say!

271
00:27:38,521 --> 00:27:40,304
Off with ye, damned brat!

272
00:27:40,347 --> 00:27:43,304
What's your problem,
ya stubborn old fart?!

273
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:53,913
Does the dojo bore you?

274
00:27:54,435 --> 00:27:56,304
lost to Kuina again!

275
00:27:56,696 --> 00:27:59,609
I gotta practice more!

276
00:28:02,608 --> 00:28:04,173
Huh?!

277
00:28:04,608 --> 00:28:06,478
I don't got money to pay with, though!

278
00:28:06,913 --> 00:28:09,000
They are yours.

279
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,782
Blunt as they are, though.

280
00:28:13,782 --> 00:28:15,173
I...

281
00:28:15,174 --> 00:28:19,260
...cannot seem to forge
anything but junk in my old age.

282
00:28:19,913 --> 00:28:22,000
Use them for your training.

283
00:28:28,869 --> 00:28:30,304
Listen, now.

284
00:28:30,304 --> 00:28:32,825
A sword is like a kitchen knife,
but for murder!

285
00:28:33,304 --> 00:28:35,869
They are designed to kill people!

286
00:28:39,086 --> 00:28:45,695
A swordsmith hones their craft so that their weapons
are better at killing than any other!

287
00:28:47,217 --> 00:28:49,826
Every sword possesses
its own personality;

288
00:28:49,826 --> 00:28:53,826
'tis a swordsman's lot to tame it!

289
00:28:54,478 --> 00:28:57,478
And they label dangerous
swords "cursed?!

290
00:28:58,739 --> 00:29:02,217
Ridiculous!
That is the hallmark of a fine sword!

291
00:29:02,652 --> 00:29:06,565
If the weak fear it
and deem it "cursed,"

292
00:29:07,217 --> 00:29:08,521
it is rather...

293
00:29:08,652 --> 00:29:10,261
...an honor!

294
00:29:10,652 --> 00:29:12,826
Swords are fearsome...

295
00:29:12,826 --> 00:29:17,565
...because they yearn
so deeply to be deadly!

296
00:29:21,174 --> 00:29:25,782
There was one I forged
when I was young...

297
00:29:25,782 --> 00:29:30,260
And it was my greatest
stroke of genius...

298
00:29:31,652 --> 00:29:33,522
The sword had
a serious temperament!

299
00:29:34,391 --> 00:29:41,521
'Twas such a fine blade,
it gave you chills merely from holding it...

300
00:29:44,043 --> 00:29:47,695
And to it, I gave the name of
hell's mighty king!

301
00:30:00,957 --> 00:30:04,217
Hell's mighty king...

302
00:30:12,608 --> 00:30:13,869
Enma!

303
00:30:16,521 --> 00:30:19,043
My village was named Shimotsuki...

304
00:30:19,652 --> 00:30:21,913
Guess it wasn't a coincidence...

305
00:30:23,217 --> 00:30:27,043
On the day that old man died,
learned...

306
00:30:27,043 --> 00:30:29,303
...that he was Kuina's grandfather.

307
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:47,435
Catch me if you want
this Excellent Grade Sword back!

308
00:30:47,435 --> 00:30:51,304
That's just a bamboo sword!
Give it back, darn it!

309
00:30:51,304 --> 00:30:53,912
Hey, guys! Did you know?!

310
00:30:53,913 --> 00:30:58,565
My grandma said this village
was founded by a pirate!

311
00:30:58,565 --> 00:30:59,825
Whaaaa!!

312
00:31:00,435 --> 00:31:02,304
A pirate...

313
00:31:04,217 --> 00:31:07,434
The artisan,
Shimotsuki Kozaburo!

314
00:31:07,435 --> 00:31:12,521
More than half a century ago,
he unlawfully emigrated from this country.

315
00:31:12,521 --> 00:31:16,478
That old man was a samurai
from the Land of Wano?!

316
00:31:17,739 --> 00:31:21,217
The swordsmith,
Shimotsuki Kozaburo!

317
00:31:21,217 --> 00:31:24,043
Finer swords closely observe humans!

318
00:31:24,043 --> 00:31:27,651
They select their swordsmen!

319
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:32,957
They say the sword chooses the owner.

320
00:31:45,086 --> 00:31:46,608
You came to me...

321
00:31:46,608 --> 00:31:50,391
...because you chose me,
you wanted to test me...

322
00:31:56,217 --> 00:32:01,043
A sword is honest, direct...
Not evil.

323
00:32:05,652 --> 00:32:09,087
That means it's my strength
that's lacking!

324
00:32:11,174 --> 00:32:15,913
So does this mean that
even with you draining a ton of Haki,

325
00:32:15,913 --> 00:32:18,348
Oden wielded you like
you were light as a feather?

326
00:32:19,043 --> 00:32:21,695
Am I right, Enma?

327
00:32:27,043 --> 00:32:30,434
There he is!
It's Pirate Hunter Zoro!

328
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:32,435
And he's all beat up!

329
00:32:32,435 --> 00:32:34,521
King-san!

330
00:32:34,521 --> 00:32:37,869
Let us take his head!

331
00:32:37,869 --> 00:32:39,912
If we beat him, we'll get promoted!

332
00:32:39,957 --> 00:32:42,261
Me! I'll do it!

333
00:32:46,043 --> 00:32:48,129
What do I do...

334
00:32:48,521 --> 00:32:50,956
...to keep my Haki in balance?

335
00:32:52,478 --> 00:32:56,391
I'm dead if I keep releasing
this much Haki...

336
00:33:01,130 --> 00:33:02,130
NO...

337
00:33:08,391 --> 00:33:10,217
I'm fine with that!

338
00:33:14,478 --> 00:33:15,608
I see...

339
00:33:17,391 --> 00:33:19,695
Looking to become a king?

340
00:33:26,826 --> 00:33:29,999
That sounds great!
The world's greatest swordsman?

341
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:34,826
The Pirate King won't settle
for anything less!

342
00:33:37,435 --> 00:33:38,652
That's right.

343
00:33:40,478 --> 00:33:42,217
'Cause I've got...

344
00:33:42,913 --> 00:33:44,696
...promises to keep...

345
00:33:45,913 --> 00:33:48,478
...to my captain,
and to my best friend!